---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { business } from '../data/site.js';

// Linked from the Shift4 payment link checkout page as the Terms & Conditions
// URL. Shift4 branding settings are account-wide, so this page has to cover
// every kind of advance purchase we take, not just one event.
const updated = 'November 19, 2026';

const h2 = "font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;color:var(--gold-light);font-size:1.4rem;margin:2rem 0 0.6rem;";
---

<Base
  title="Payment & Ticket Terms | Just Enuff Cabaret, Rockford IL"
  description="Terms for advance ticket, package, and event purchases from Just Enuff Cabaret in Rockford, IL. Redemption, refunds, age requirements, and entry conditions."
>
  <div class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
    <h1 class="page-title">Payment &amp; Ticket <em>Terms</em></h1>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <p class="lead">Last updated {updated}</p>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="inner-sm" style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;color:var(--grey);font-size:1.1rem;line-height:1.7;">
      <p>
        These terms apply when you buy a ticket, package, event admission, or other item
        from {business.name} in advance, whether through a payment link, in person, or over
        the phone. By completing a purchase you agree to these terms.
      </p>

      <h2 style={h2}>Age Requirement</h2>
      <p>
        You must be 21 or older to enter our venue or to redeem any purchase. Entry requires a
        valid, unexpired government-issued photo ID. There are no exceptions, and purchasing in
        advance does not waive this requirement. If you cannot present valid ID, you will not be
        admitted and your purchase will not be refunded.
      </p>

      <h2 style={h2}>How to Redeem an Advance Purchase</h2>
      <p>
        When your payment is complete you will receive a receipt by email. To redeem, bring that
        receipt with you, on your phone or printed, along with a photo ID matching the name on
        the receipt. We check each purchase against our records at the door.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each purchase admits one guest unless the item description says otherwise. A receipt may
        be redeemed one time only. If you bought a package for someone else, call us at
        <a href={business.phoneHref} style="color:var(--gold);"> {business.phone}</a> before the
        event date so we can note the guest's name, otherwise we may not be able to honor it at
        the door.
      </p>

      <h2 style={h2}>Refunds &amp; Cancellations</h2>
      <p>
        <strong style="color:var(--cream);">Advance purchases are final and non-refundable.</strong>
        This includes situations where you change your mind, do not attend, arrive after the
        event has ended, or are unable to present the required receipt or ID.
      </p>
      <p>
        If we cancel an event outright, we will refund the amount you paid to the original payment
        method. If we reschedule an event, your purchase will be honored on the new date, and you
        may request a refund instead by contacting us before that new date.
      </p>

      <h2 style={h2}>Availability &amp; Changes</h2>
      <p>
        Advance purchases are limited in number and are sold on a first-come basis. Once an
        allotment sells out, the payment link closes. We may change the lineup, menu items,
        entertainers, timing, or specific components of an event where circumstances require it.
        We will make reasonable efforts to provide a substitute of comparable value, and such
        changes are not grounds for a refund.
      </p>
      <p>
        Prices shown at checkout are in US dollars and do not include gratuity. Advance pricing
        applies only until the cutoff time stated at checkout. After that time, standard pricing
        at the door applies.
      </p>

      <h2 style={h2}>Entry &amp; Conduct</h2>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to refuse entry or to remove any guest, consistent with applicable
        law, including for intoxication, disorderly or threatening behavior, harassment of our
        entertainers or staff, or violation of our house rules. If you are refused entry or
        removed for any of these reasons, your purchase will not be refunded.
      </p>
      <p>
        Entry may also be subject to capacity limits set by law or by local authorities. If
        capacity prevents us from admitting you despite a valid advance purchase, we will refund
        you in full.
      </p>

      <h2 style={h2}>Payment Processing</h2>
      <p>
        Card payments are processed by our payment provider. We do not receive or store your full
        card number. The name, billing address, and email address you enter at checkout are used
        to process the payment, to send your receipt, and to verify your purchase at the door.
        See our <a href="/privacy-policy" style="color:var(--gold);">Privacy Policy</a> for how we
        handle that information.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your card statement will show a charge from {business.name} or our payment provider. If
        you believe a charge is incorrect, please contact us first at
        <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`} style="color:var(--gold);"> {business.email}</a> or
        <a href={business.phoneHref} style="color:var(--gold);"> {business.phone}</a>. We will
        review it promptly, and most issues are resolved faster this way than through your bank.
      </p>

      <h2 style={h2}>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {business.name}<br />
        {business.address.street}, {business.address.city}, {business.address.state} {business.address.zip}<br />
        <a href={business.phoneHref} style="color:var(--gold);">{business.phone}</a> ·
        <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`} style="color:var(--gold);"> {business.email}</a>
      </p>

      <p style="margin-top:2rem;font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--grey);">
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Illinois. This page is provided for
        general informational purposes and is not legal advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
